<description>
Replace masked pixels with the unique visible color from the same symmetry orbit.

Input structure:
- The grid is square.
- One color marks unknown cells and is the only color whose removal makes all
  symmetry orbits internally consistent.
- The underlying image is invariant under main-diagonal transpose and under
  row/column reflection of the trailing square after a leading prefix.

Rule:
- Infer the leading prefix length, the mask color, and the corresponding
  symmetry orbits.
- For every orbit containing masked pixels, replace them with the orbit's
  unique non-mask color.
- Preserve all already visible pixels.

Key insight:
- The mask is transparent damage over a dihedral-symmetric pattern, so even
  cells whose transpose is also masked are determined by another orbit mate.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "grid with one mask color over a pattern symmetric by main-diagonal transpose and by row/column reflection after a two-row/two-column prefix",
  "transform": "replace each mask pixel with the unique non-mask color in its symmetry orbit; preserve all visible pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 30x30 square [observed]
  underlying_pattern:
    symmetry: full-grid transpose (o==o.T) plus D4 (all 8 dihedral) on trailing block
    margin: 2 [observed] -- first 2 rows/cols form prefix; remaining 28x28 is the trailing block
    trailing_block: 28x28 with LR, UD, diagonal, and anti-diagonal reflective symmetry (equivalently rot90+reflections)
    prefix: rows 0-1 and cols 0-1 are related only by transpose; not reflected
    fundamental_domain: upper-left triangle of upper-left 14x14 quadrant of trailing block, plus 2x2 corner and one prefix strip
    colors: 9 colors (0-8); color 0 is background at 32-68% of pixels; 8 non-bg colors each occupy 1-20 orbits
  mask:
    color: 9 -- absent from output; always the 10th color
    pixel_count: 49-123 (5-14% of grid)
    blob_count: 2-5 contiguous 4-connected components
    blob_sizes: 4-60 pixels each
    constraint: every orbit containing mask pixels must retain >=1 non-mask pixel (max mask fraction per orbit <=0.50)
    distribution: may appear in prefix and/or trailing regions; never in 2x2 corner [observed]
  transform: replace each mask pixel with the unique non-mask color of its symmetry orbit

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size 30 and margin 2.
    2. Build the output pattern with full D4 symmetry on the 28x28 trailing block and transpose symmetry on the full 30x30 grid. Assign colors 0-8 to orbits; background (0) should cover ~40-65% of orbits; each of 8 non-bg colors gets >=1 orbit.
    3. Place mask (color 9) over 2-5 contiguous rectangular-ish blobs totaling 49-123 pixels. For each affected orbit, mask at most half its pixels so at least one non-mask member survives. Replace chosen output pixels with 9 to produce the input.
    4. Verify solver can uniquely infer margin and mask color (the assert in _infer_margin_and_mask).
```
